IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maca-core`

-- Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NT) -- the questions of those left after a death in a motor accident.
--
-- SEAT: on a death, the people Part 5 pays: the spouse of the person who died, a dependent child (or whoever asks for the child),
-- a dependent parent, and the person liable to meet the expense of the funeral. "Do death benefits apply? Am I a spouse, a dependent
-- child or a dependent parent? Are death benefits excluded, or may they be reduced? How much is the funeral benefit, the lump sum and
-- my share, the children's weekly benefit, the parents' benefit? By when must I claim?" Facts about the person who died, and about
-- the accident, are ones a member of the family could state. Where the Act leaves a judgment to the Commission (dependency, a
-- reduction under s 20A), the question asks what the Commission decided. The rules are in maca-core.l4; this module restates none.
-- Every name here differs from the names in maca-seat.l4, so a case file can import both seats.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY. Quotations of the Act and Regulations in maca-core.l4 are not an official version. Copyright in Northern Territory
-- legislation is owned by the Northern Territory (NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996; owner's ruling of 24 October 2026).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NT) -- questions after a death`

§§ `ss 7, 20 -- do death benefits apply`

DECLARE `Death benefits answer` IS ONE OF
    `death benefits apply: a death from a motor accident in the Territory (ss 7(1), 20(a))`
    `death benefits apply: a Territory resident, in a motor accident elsewhere in Australia arising out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (ss 7(2), 20(b))`
    `no death benefits: the person who died was a qualifying person (s 20(b)), but the accident happened outside Australia (s 7(2)(a))`
    `no death benefits` HAS `because` IS AN `Entitlement answer`
    `no death benefits: the death did not result from injuries received in the motor accident (s 20)`

@export Do the motor accidents scheme's death benefits apply to this death (ss 4A, 4B, 7, 20)?
GIVEN `the death resulted from injuries in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person died as a result of injuries received in the accident
      `the vehicle was self-propelled, or a trailer attached to one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle involved was designed to be self-propelled (a car, motorbike, truck, bus and the like), or was a trailer attached to such a vehicle
      `the vehicle runs on rails` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was one that runs on rails, such as a train or tram
      `the vehicle is a slow motorised wheelchair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was a motorised wheelchair that cannot travel faster than 10 km/h
      `the vehicle is a cycle with an engine of 200 watts or less` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was a cycle powered by an engine of no more than 200 watts
      `the accident came directly from the vehicle being driven` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted directly from the driving of the vehicle
      `the accident came directly from the vehicle moving out of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted directly from the vehicle moving out of control
      `the accident came directly from a collision with the vehicle or from avoiding one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident resulted directly from a collision with the vehicle, moving or stationary, or from action to avoid one
      `they were hurt in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was injured in, or as a result of, the accident itself
      `they were hurt helping at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was injured while helping, or trying to help, at the scene of a motor accident
      `the accident happened in the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in the Northern Territory
      `the accident happened in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in Australia (answer yes for an accident in the Territory)
      `a Territory-registered vehicle was in use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident involved, and arose out of the use of, a vehicle currently registered in the Northern Territory
      `they had lived in the Territory for at least 3 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the accident, the person who died had lived in the Northern Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months
      `they were not living in the Territory at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, the person who died was not living in the Northern Territory
      `they had been living outside the Territory for 6 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died had been living outside the Northern Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more
      `their main home or main job was outside the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the primary dwelling house or primary employment of the person who died was outside the Northern Territory
      `they had left the Territory meaning to live elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died had left the Northern Territory intending no longer to live there
      `damages for the death have been claimed where it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident outside the Territory: whether damages or compensation for the death have been claimed under the law of the State or Territory where it happened
GIVETH A `Death benefits answer`
DECIDE `Do death benefits apply` IS
    IF NOT `the death resulted from injuries in the accident`
    THEN `no death benefits: the death did not result from injuries received in the motor accident (s 20)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the s 7 entitlement for` `their occurrence` `at` `their place` `of a person with` `their residence` `who claimed elsewhere` `damages for the death have been claimed where it happened`
         WHEN `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))` THEN `death benefits apply: a death from a motor accident in the Territory (ss 7(1), 20(a))`
         WHEN `entitled: a Territory resident, in a motor accident elsewhere in Australia arising out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2))` THEN `death benefits apply: a Territory resident, in a motor accident elsewhere in Australia arising out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (ss 7(2), 20(b))`
         WHEN `not entitled: the accident happened outside Australia (s 7(2)(a))` THEN
             IF `is a qualifying person, dying after an accident at` `their place` `being a resident` (`is a resident of the Territory` `their residence`)
             THEN `no death benefits: the person who died was a qualifying person (s 20(b)), but the accident happened outside Australia (s 7(2)(a))`
             ELSE `no death benefits` `not entitled: the accident happened outside Australia (s 7(2)(a))`
         WHEN `other` THEN `no death benefits` `other`
    WHERE
        `their occurrence` MEANS
            `Occurrence` WITH
                `the vehicle` IS `Vehicle` WITH
                    `is designed to be self-propelled, or is a trailer attached to such a vehicle` IS `the vehicle was self-propelled, or a trailer attached to one`
                    `runs on rails`                                                               IS `the vehicle runs on rails`
                    `is a motorised wheelchair not capable of more than 10 km/h`                   IS `the vehicle is a slow motorised wheelchair`
                    `is a cycle powered by an engine of no more than 200 watts`                    IS `the vehicle is a cycle with an engine of 200 watts or less`
                `resulted directly from the driving of the vehicle`                                    IS `the accident came directly from the vehicle being driven`
                `resulted directly from the vehicle moving out of control`                             IS `the accident came directly from the vehicle moving out of control`
                `resulted directly from a collision, or action to avoid a collision, with the vehicle` IS `the accident came directly from a collision with the vehicle or from avoiding one`
                `the person was killed or injured in it`                                               IS `they were hurt in the accident`
                `the person was killed or injured rendering assistance at the scene`                   IS `they were hurt helping at the scene`
        `their place` MEANS
            `Accident place` WITH
                `occurred in the Territory`                         IS `the accident happened in the Territory`
                `occurred in Australia`                             IS `the accident happened in Australia`
                `arose out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle` IS `a Territory-registered vehicle was in use`
        `their residence` MEANS
            `Residence` WITH
                `had resided in the Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months`        IS `they had lived in the Territory for at least 3 months in a row`
                `was not living in the Territory at the time`                                      IS `they were not living in the Territory at the time`
                `had been living outside the Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more` IS `they had been living outside the Territory for 6 months or more`
                `primary dwelling house or primary employment was not in the Territory`            IS `their main home or main job was outside the Territory`
                `had left the Territory intending no longer to reside there`                       IS `they had left the Territory meaning to live elsewhere`

§§ `s 4 -- spouse, dependent child, dependent parent`

@export Am I the spouse of the person who died, for the motor accidents scheme (s 4)?
GIVEN `I was married to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married to the person who died
      `I was their de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the de facto partner of the person who died
      `we were living together as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the death, you were living with them on a genuine domestic basis
      `we had been de facto partners for 2 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had been their de facto partner for a continuous period of at least 2 years immediately before the death
      `the Commission considers I was dependent on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that you were wholly or substantially dependent on the person who died
      `we were married by Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander custom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the person who died are Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islanders married according to the customs and traditions of your community
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the spouse of the person who died` IF
    `is a spouse within s 4` (`Partner` WITH
        `was married to the person`                                                                  IS `I was married to them`
        `was the person's de facto partner`                                                          IS `I was their de facto partner`
        `was living with the person on a bona fide domestic basis`                                   IS `we were living together as a couple`
        `had been the de facto partner for a continuous period of at least 2 years immediately before` IS `we had been de facto partners for 2 years or more`
        `the Commission considers them wholly or substantially dependent on the person`              IS `the Commission considers I was dependent on them`
        `both are Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islanders married by the customs of their community`   IS `we were married by Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander custom`)

@export Is this child a dependent child of the person who died, for the motor accidents scheme (s 4)?
GIVEN `they are the child of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a child of the person who died, including an unborn child or a child to whom the person stood in the place of a parent
      `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in completed years (at the death for the lump sum; in the week asked about for the weekly benefit)
      `the child is a full-time student or has a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a full-time student, or physically or mentally handicapped
      `the child is someone's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is the spouse of another person
      `the child depended on them financially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was dependent on the person who died for financial support (for an unborn child, whether that was reasonably expected)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this child a dependent child of the person who died` IF
    `is a dependent child within s 4` (`Child` WITH
        `is the person's child, unborn child or a child to whom the person stood in loco parentis` IS `they are the child of the person who died`
        `age in completed years`                                                                 IS `the child's age`
        `is a full-time student, or physically or mentally handicapped`                           IS `the child is a full-time student or has a disability`
        `is the spouse of another person`                                                        IS `the child is someone's spouse`
        `is dependent on the person for financial support, or for an unborn child is expected to be` IS `the child depended on them financially`)

@export Am I a dependent parent of the person who died, for the motor accidents scheme (s 4)?
GIVEN `I am their parent or a listed relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent, adoptive parent, step-parent, grandparent, or parent of the spouse, of the person who died
      `I depended mainly on them financially at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, you were primarily dependent on the person who died for financial support
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a dependent parent of the person who died` IF
    `is a dependent parent within s 4, being` `I am their parent or a listed relative` `and` `I depended mainly on them financially at the accident`

§§ `Part 3, s 20A -- are death benefits excluded or reduced`

DECLARE `Death exclusion answer` IS ONE OF
    `death benefits are excluded` HAS `under` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `death benefits are not excluded by Part 3`
    `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014 (s 46)`

@export Are death benefits excluded because of how the accident happened, or how the person who died was involved (ss 9D-9G, 10-10C)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (Part 3 as encoded applies to accidents on or after 1 July 2014)
      `they were driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was driving a motor vehicle in the accident
      `the Commission considers it was an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency
      `they were in a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was in a motor vehicle in the accident
      `they owned that vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died owned the vehicle they were in
      `it had been unregistered for 3 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that vehicle was unregistered and had been for at least 3 months
      `it was a vehicle that could not be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that vehicle was of a kind prescribed by reg 4B (for example a pre-1971 vehicle that cannot meet safety standards, or one never given a compliance plate)
      `they knew or should have known it was unregistered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as its driver, the person who died knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was unregistered
      `it was conditionally registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that vehicle was registered subject to conditions or restrictions
      `they knew or should have known it was conditionally registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as its driver, the person who died knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was conditionally registered
      `it was driven in breach of its registration conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that vehicle was being driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions of its registration
      `another registered vehicle being driven lawfully was involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident involved another vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions
      `they stole or unlawfully used a vehicle involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use of a vehicle involved
      `they were using a vehicle for an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was using a vehicle involved for, or in connection with, an indictable offence
      `they were using a vehicle to escape or avoid arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was using a vehicle involved to escape from an offence, or to avoid apprehension or detention
      `they were using a vehicle intending to cause death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was using a vehicle involved intending to inflict death or injury on themself or another
      `the death is covered by workers compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death is compensable under the Return to Work Act 1986 (NT) or another workers compensation law, or would be but for self-infliction or serious and wilful misconduct
      `a vehicle in the accident was in a motor sport event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a vehicle involved was taking part in a motor sport event
      `they were in that vehicle or involved in the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was the driver of or a passenger in that vehicle, or an official, organiser, helper or otherwise associated with the event
      `the accident was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act
GIVETH A `Death exclusion answer`
DECIDE `Are death benefits excluded` IS
    CONSIDER `the exclusion`
    WHEN `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and Part 3 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 46)` THEN `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014 (s 46)`
    WHEN `no benefits are payable at all` `under` THEN `death benefits are excluded` `under`
    WHEN `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` `under` THEN `death benefits are excluded` `under`
    OTHERWISE `death benefits are not excluded by Part 3`
    WHERE
        `the exclusion` MEANS
            `the Part 3 exclusion for` (`Part 3 facts` WITH
                `the day of the accident`                                                                       IS `the day of the accident`
                `was driving a motor vehicle`                                                                   IS `they were driving`
                -- The fields for ss 9-9C (alcohol, conduct, risk, licence) are fixed placeholders: those sections reach only
                -- compensation for loss of earning capacity and the impairment lump sum, never death benefits.
                `was under the influence of alcohol or a drug to the extent of committing a road traffic offence` IS FALSE
                `the alcohol readings` IS `Alcohol readings` WITH
                    `the highest breath alcohol concentration, in grams per 210 litres`                                  IS 0
                    `the highest blood alcohol concentration from a sample within 4 hours, in grams per 100 millilitres` IS 0
                    `failed to submit to a breath analysis or provide a blood sample when required`                      IS FALSE
                    `the Commission is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse for that failure`                         IS FALSE
                `the Commission is of the opinion that the alcohol or drug contributed to the accident`          IS FALSE
                `it is established that the alcohol did not contribute to the accident`                         IS FALSE
                `the Commission is of the opinion that the person's conduct contributed to the accident`         IS FALSE
                `has been found guilty, for that conduct, of manslaughter, an offence of seriously harming or endangering others, or dangerous driving` IS FALSE
                `was engaged in conduct that created a substantial risk of injury to themself and recklessly ignored the risk` IS FALSE
                `had never held a licence for that class of motor vehicle`                                       IS FALSE
                `the licence was suspended, other than to enforce a fine or penalty`                            IS FALSE
                `the licence had been cancelled`                                                                IS FALSE
                `the licence had lapsed or expired at least 3 months before the accident`                       IS FALSE
                `was driving in breach of the conditions of the licence`                                        IS FALSE
                `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`            IS `the Commission considers it was an emergency`
                `was in a motor vehicle`                                                                        IS `they were in a motor vehicle`
                `was the owner of that motor vehicle`                                                           IS `they owned that vehicle`
                `that vehicle was unregistered and had been for at least 3 months`                              IS `it had been unregistered for 3 months or more`
                `that vehicle was of a kind prescribed by reg 4B`                                               IS `it was a vehicle that could not be registered`
                `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was unregistered`                                 IS `they knew or should have known it was unregistered`
                `that vehicle was conditionally registered`                                                     IS `it was conditionally registered`
                `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was conditionally registered`                     IS `they knew or should have known it was conditionally registered`
                `that vehicle was being driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions of its registration` IS `it was driven in breach of its registration conditions`
                `the accident involved another motor vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions` IS `another registered vehicle being driven lawfully was involved`
                `was criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use of a motor vehicle involved`          IS `they stole or unlawfully used a vehicle involved`
                `was using a motor vehicle involved for, or in connection with, an indictable offence`           IS `they were using a vehicle for an indictable offence`
                `was using a motor vehicle involved to escape from an offence or to avoid apprehension or detention` IS `they were using a vehicle to escape or avoid arrest`
                `was using a motor vehicle involved intending to inflict death or injury on themself or another` IS `they were using a vehicle intending to cause death or injury`
                `the injury or death is compensable under workers compensation legislation, or would be but for self-infliction or serious and wilful misconduct` IS `the death is covered by workers compensation`
                `a motor vehicle involved was taking part in a motor sport event`                               IS `a vehicle in the accident was in a motor sport event`
                `was its driver or passenger, or an official or organiser of the event, or assisting or otherwise associated with it` IS `they were in that vehicle or involved in the event`
                `it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act`                              IS `the accident was a terrorist act`)

@export May the Commission reduce death benefits because the person who died was driving affected by alcohol or a drug, or recklessly ignored a risk (s 20A; reg 4M)?
GIVEN `they were driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was driving a motor vehicle in the accident
      `they were over the limit for alcohol or drugs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was under the influence of alcohol or a drug to the extent that driving was (or on a public street would have been) a road traffic offence
      `their highest breath alcohol reading` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest breath alcohol concentration from a breath analysis under the Traffic Act 1987, in grams per 210 litres of breath; 0 if none
      `their highest blood alcohol reading` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest blood alcohol concentration from a blood sample taken within 4 hours of the accident, in grams per 100 millilitres; 0 if none
      `the Commission considers the alcohol or drug contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that the alcohol or drug contributed to the accident (asked where no presumption arises)
      `it has been shown the alcohol did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been established that the alcohol did not contribute to the accident
      `they recklessly ignored a substantial risk to themself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died, as driver, passenger, cyclist, pedestrian or otherwise, was doing something that created a substantial risk of injury to themself and recklessly ignored it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May death benefits be reduced under s 20A` IF
    `the Commission may reduce death benefits under s 20A for` (`Part 3 facts` WITH
        -- Only the fields ss 9 and 9B read (through s 20A(1), (3)) are asked; the others are fixed placeholders.
        `the day of the accident`                                                                       IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2014
        `was driving a motor vehicle`                                                                   IS `they were driving`
        `was under the influence of alcohol or a drug to the extent of committing a road traffic offence` IS `they were over the limit for alcohol or drugs`
        `the alcohol readings` IS `Alcohol readings` WITH
            `the highest breath alcohol concentration, in grams per 210 litres`                                  IS `their highest breath alcohol reading`
            `the highest blood alcohol concentration from a sample within 4 hours, in grams per 100 millilitres` IS `their highest blood alcohol reading`
            -- Reg 4M(5) (a person who fails to give a sample) is not asked after a death.
            `failed to submit to a breath analysis or provide a blood sample when required`                      IS FALSE
            `the Commission is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse for that failure`                         IS FALSE
        `the Commission is of the opinion that the alcohol or drug contributed to the accident`          IS `the Commission considers the alcohol or drug contributed`
        `it is established that the alcohol did not contribute to the accident`                         IS `it has been shown the alcohol did not contribute`
        `the Commission is of the opinion that the person's conduct contributed to the accident`         IS FALSE
        `has been found guilty, for that conduct, of manslaughter, an offence of seriously harming or endangering others, or dangerous driving` IS FALSE
        `was engaged in conduct that created a substantial risk of injury to themself and recklessly ignored the risk` IS `they recklessly ignored a substantial risk to themself`
        `had never held a licence for that class of motor vehicle`                                       IS FALSE
        `the licence was suspended, other than to enforce a fine or penalty`                            IS FALSE
        `the licence had been cancelled`                                                                IS FALSE
        `the licence had lapsed or expired at least 3 months before the accident`                       IS FALSE
        `was driving in breach of the conditions of the licence`                                        IS FALSE
        `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`            IS FALSE
        `was in a motor vehicle`                                                                        IS FALSE
        `was the owner of that motor vehicle`                                                           IS FALSE
        `that vehicle was unregistered and had been for at least 3 months`                              IS FALSE
        `that vehicle was of a kind prescribed by reg 4B`                                               IS FALSE
        `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was unregistered`                                 IS FALSE
        `that vehicle was conditionally registered`                                                     IS FALSE
        `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was conditionally registered`                     IS FALSE
        `that vehicle was being driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions of its registration` IS FALSE
        `the accident involved another motor vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions` IS FALSE
        `was criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use of a motor vehicle involved`          IS FALSE
        `was using a motor vehicle involved for, or in connection with, an indictable offence`           IS FALSE
        `was using a motor vehicle involved to escape from an offence or to avoid apprehension or detention` IS FALSE
        `was using a motor vehicle involved intending to inflict death or injury on themself or another` IS FALSE
        `the injury or death is compensable under workers compensation legislation, or would be but for self-infliction or serious and wilful misconduct` IS FALSE
        `a motor vehicle involved was taking part in a motor sport event`                               IS FALSE
        `was its driver or passenger, or an official or organiser of the event, or assisting or otherwise associated with it` IS FALSE
        `it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act`                              IS FALSE)

@export Are the funeral benefit, the death lump sum and the children's weekly benefit reduced by 25% because the person who died was not wearing a seatbelt or helmet (s 11)?
GIVEN `their date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who died (s 11 applies only to a person 16 or older at the accident)
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was not wearing a seatbelt or safety helmet that the Traffic Act 1987 (or the law where the accident happened) required, with no exemption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are death benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` IF
    `s 11 applies to a person of` (`the age of a person born` `their date of birth` `on` `the day of the accident`) `who` `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet`

§§ `ss 22-24, 37 -- how much`

@export How much is the funeral benefit for the person liable to pay for the funeral, if Part 3 leaves it payable (ss 11, 11A, 22(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the cost of the funeral` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost of the funeral, in dollars
      `Territory average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Territory average weekly earnings for the calendar year of payment: the ABS full-time adult ordinary time earnings for the Northern Territory last published before 1 January, in dollars
      `their date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who died
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was not wearing a seatbelt or safety helmet the law required, with no exemption
      `other insurance set against the funeral benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount of other insurance or compensation (not workers compensation) for the death that the Commission sets against this benefit, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the funeral benefit` IS
    `the s 22(1)(a) funeral benefit for a funeral costing` `the cost of the funeral` `at average weekly earnings of` `Territory average weekly earnings` `with s 11` (`s 11 applies to a person of` (`the age of a person born` `their date of birth` `on` `the day of the accident`) `who` `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet`) `less` `other insurance set against the funeral benefit`

@export How much is the death lump sum for the spouse and dependent children, and each one's share, if Part 3 leaves it payable (ss 11, 11A, 20A, 22(1)(b), (3), (4), 37)?
GIVEN `Territory average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Territory average weekly earnings for the calendar year of payment: the ABS full-time adult ordinary time earnings for the Northern Territory last published before 1 January, in dollars
      `there is a surviving spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died left a spouse (see the spouse question)
      `the number of spouses` IS A NUMBER @desc How many spouses the person who died left: 1, or more only for an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander married to more than one person by custom (s 37)
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children the person who died left (see the dependent child question); 0 if none
      `the impairment lump sum they had been paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Any lump sum for permanent impairment from the same injury paid to the person before they died, in dollars; 0 if none
      `their date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who died
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was not wearing a seatbelt or safety helmet the law required, with no exemption
      `the s 20A reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The proportion by which the Commission has decided to reduce death benefits under s 20A, as a fraction (for example 0.2 for 20%); 0 if none
      `other insurance set against the lump sum` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount of other insurance or compensation (not workers compensation) for the death that the Commission sets against this lump sum, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A `Death lump sum answer`
DECIDE `How much is the death lump sum` IS
    `the s 22(1)(b) lump sum for` (`Death lump sum facts` WITH
        `average weekly earnings when the payment is made`                         IS `Territory average weekly earnings`
        `there is a spouse`                                                        IS `there is a surviving spouse`
        `the number of spouses (s 37)`                                             IS `the number of spouses`
        `the number of dependent children`                                         IS `the number of dependent children`
        `the impairment lump sum the qualifying person received for the same injury` IS `the impairment lump sum they had been paid`
        `s 11 applies`                                                             IS `s 11 applies to a person of` (`the age of a person born` `their date of birth` `on` `the day of the accident`) `who` `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet`
        `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined`                            IS `the s 20A reduction`
        `the s 11A entitlement set against it`                                     IS `other insurance set against the lump sum`)

@export How much is the weekly benefit for each dependent child, on top of the lump sum, if Part 3 leaves it payable (ss 11, 11A, 20A, 23)?
GIVEN `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children the person who died left (see the dependent child question)
      `Territory average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Territory average weekly earnings for the calendar year of payment: the ABS full-time adult ordinary time earnings for the Northern Territory last published before 1 January, in dollars
      `their date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who died
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident
      `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was not wearing a seatbelt or safety helmet the law required, with no exemption
      `the s 20A reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The proportion by which the Commission has decided to reduce death benefits under s 20A, as a fraction (for example 0.2 for 20%); 0 if none
      `other insurance set against each child's week` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount of other insurance or compensation (not workers compensation) the Commission sets against each child's weekly payment, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is each dependent child's weekly benefit` IS
    `the s 23 weekly benefit for each of` `the number of dependent children` `children at average weekly earnings of` `Territory average weekly earnings` `with s 11` (`s 11 applies to a person of` (`the age of a person born` `their date of birth` `on` `the day of the accident`) `who` `they were not wearing a required seatbelt or helmet`) `and s 20A` `the s 20A reduction` `less` `other insurance set against each child's week`

@export If the person who died left no spouse and no dependent child, how much does each dependent parent who lived with them get, if Part 3 leaves it payable (ss 11A, 20A, 24)?
GIVEN `they left a spouse or a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died left a spouse or a dependent child
      `the number of dependent parents living with them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent parents normally lived with the person who died (see the dependent parent question)
      `Territory average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Territory average weekly earnings for the calendar year of payment: the ABS full-time adult ordinary time earnings for the Northern Territory last published before 1 January, in dollars
      `the s 20A reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The proportion by which the Commission has decided to reduce death benefits under s 20A, as a fraction (for example 0.2 for 20%); 0 if none
      `other insurance set against the parents' benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount of other insurance or compensation (not workers compensation) for the death that the Commission sets against this benefit, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does each dependent parent get` IS
    `the s 24 benefit for each dependent parent, with a spouse or child surviving` `they left a spouse or a dependent child` `and` `the number of dependent parents living with them` `parents, at average weekly earnings of` `Territory average weekly earnings` `with s 20A` `the s 20A reduction` `less` `other insurance set against the parents' benefit`

§§ `s 21 -- a spouse permanently in hospital` -- only if the injured person is not expected ever to leave hospital

@export My spouse was injured in a motor accident and will probably never leave hospital: can the Commission, on my written request, treat them as having died so that death benefits are paid (s 21)?
GIVEN `they would be a qualifying person had they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse would have been a qualifying person had they died: injured in a motor accident in the Territory, or a Territory resident injured elsewhere in a motor accident involving a Territory vehicle
      `they are a full-time patient because of the injuries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse is a full-time patient in a hospital or other institution because of the injuries
      `the Commission considers they will probably remain one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is of the opinion that your spouse is likely to remain a full-time patient permanently
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my spouse be treated as having died` IF
    `the Commission may apply Part 5 on the spouse's written request (s 21), where` `they would be a qualifying person had they died` `and` `they are a full-time patient because of the injuries` `and` `the Commission considers they will probably remain one`

§§ `s 31 -- making a claim after a death`

@export What is the last day I can claim death benefits before the Commission must refuse the claim as too late (s 31(3))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident in which the person was fatally injured
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, as the person claiming (a claimant under 18 at the accident has until 3 years after turning 18)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day to claim death benefits` IS
    `the last day for a claim the Commission must not refuse, for an accident on` `the day of the accident` `and a claimant born` `my date of birth`
